        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Painting a concrete floor typically costs roughly $0.30 to $0.80 per square foot if you do it yourself and roughly $2 to $5 per square foot if you hire it out, which puts a 500-square-foot basement at about $200 to $500 DIY or $1,000 to $2,500 professionally. Prep, old coatings, cracks and moisture move those numbers more than the paint does.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Paint is the cheapest way to finish concrete up front, and in a dry basement or on a covered porch it is often the cheapest over time too. In a garage with daily parking, or on a damp slab, run the lifetime numbers against epoxy or stain before you buy. Prices vary by region and change over time, so use these ranges to sanity-check local quotes, not replace them.
          </p>
